{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795773954,"nonce":"uIqm+dhAtYzweKy9UxComM5reeQ=","title":"A shadow with no colour is black instead of the text colour","message":"CSS gives a box-shadow, text-shadow or drop-shadow() without a colour the element's currentColor. Blinc made it black. drop-shadow() also required a blur and defaulted to half-transparent black.\n\nblinc_core::Shadow cannot grow a field while packages build it by literal, so currentColor is a colour value no stylesheet can write, Shadow::CURRENT_COLOR, put in at paint time. CSS animations and transition snapshots resolve it first, so they run between colours.","files":null}]}